{"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GettingStarted","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"image","identifier":"getting-started.png"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"By the end of this guide you will have a game with two rooms, one object, one rule, and a test that plays it. It assumes you can write basic Swift; it assumes nothing about interactive fiction."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Prefer to start from something that already runs? "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"bin\/new-game Zwank ~\/dev\/Zwank"},{"type":"text","text":" writes a complete starter package named for your game — then skim this guide for the "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"why"}]},{"type":"text","text":" behind each piece."}]},{"level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Add-Gnusto-to-your-package","text":"Add Gnusto to your package"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"These articles describe the engine on "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"main"},{"type":"text","text":", so pin the newest release: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"bin\/new-game"},{"type":"text","text":" reads it from the repository’s tags, and if a name an article uses fails to compile in your package, the pin is behind the article. Building against a checkout instead ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"bin\/new-game --dep-path"},{"type":"text","text":") cannot fall behind."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Add Gnusto as a dependency, list it in your executable target, and give the test target the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GnustoTestSupport"},{"type":"text","text":" product (it links the toolchain’s Testing library, so it belongs in test targets only):"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["\/\/ swift-tools-version: 6.2","import PackageDescription","","let package = Package(","    name: \"MyGame\",","    platforms: [.macOS(.v15)],","    dependencies: [","        .package(url: \"https:\/\/github.com\/HeirloomLogic\/Gnusto\", from: \"0.6.0\")","    ],","    targets: [","        .executableTarget(","            name: \"MyGame\",","            dependencies: [","                .product(name: \"Gnusto\", package: \"Gnusto\")","            ]","        ),","        .testTarget(","            name: \"MyGameTests\",","            dependencies: [","                \"MyGame\",","                .product(name: \"GnustoTestSupport\", package: \"Gnusto\"),","            ]","        ),","    ]",")"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Gnusto needs a Swift 6.2 toolchain and the Swift 6 language mode. The "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".macOS(.v15)"},{"type":"text","text":" floor above is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Synchronization.Mutex"},{"type":"text","text":"; Linux is tested in CI and needs no platform line. iOS is supported too, at "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".iOS(.v18)"},{"type":"text","text":" for the same reason. Add that line if your game is an app rather than a terminal program, and give it an "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/IOHandler"},{"type":"text","text":" of its own — see "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/CustomFrontEnds"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Declare-a-game","text":"Declare a game"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A game is a single type conforming to "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Game"},{"type":"text","text":". Start with just a title and an intro:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["import Gnusto","","struct MyGame: Game {","    let title = \"My First Game\"","    let intro = \"A cool breeze drifts down the hall.\"","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Game"},{"type":"text","text":" requires an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"init()"},{"type":"text","text":", but Swift synthesizes it for free as long as every stored property has a default value — which they always will here, since rooms, items, and state are declared with initializers."}]},{"level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Add-a-room","text":"Add a room"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Declare a "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Location"},{"type":"text","text":" as a stored property. The property name ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"hall"},{"type":"text","text":") becomes the room’s internal identity; the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"name(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" trait is what the player sees."}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["struct MyGame: Game {","    let title = \"My First Game\"","    let intro = \"A cool breeze drifts down the hall.\"","","    let hall = Location {","        name(\"Entrance Hall\")","        description(\"A long hall of grey stone. A doorway opens to the north.\")","    }","","    var map: WorldMap {","        player.starts(in: hall)","    }","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"map"},{"type":"text","text":" block is where geography and starting positions live. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"player.starts(in:)"},{"type":"text","text":" places the player; without it, the game has nowhere to begin."}]},{"level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Run-it","text":"Run it"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Two lines turn a game value into a running session:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let world = try GameWorld(game: MyGame())","await REPL(world: world, io: ConsoleIOHandler()).run()"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GameWorld"},{"type":"text","text":" validates the game and builds its initial state up front — a mistake like an exit to an undeclared room is caught here, as a thrown "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/BootstrapError"},{"type":"text","text":", not at runtime. "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/REPL"},{"type":"text","text":" runs the prompt\/parse\/perform\/print loop, and "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/ConsoleIOHandler"},{"type":"text","text":" reads from and writes to the terminal."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Wrap it in a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"do"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"catch"},{"type":"text","text":" in your "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"main.swift"},{"type":"text","text":":"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["import Gnusto","","do {","    let world = try GameWorld(game: MyGame())","    await REPL(world: world, io: ConsoleIOHandler()).run()","} catch {","    print(\"Couldn't start the game: \\(error)\")","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Run "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"swift run"},{"type":"text","text":", and you can already "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"look"},{"type":"text","text":" around and try to move."}]},{"level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Add-a-second-room-and-connect-them","text":"Add a second room and connect them"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Exits are declared on locations in the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"map"},{"type":"text","text":" block. Each directional method ("},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Location\/north(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Location\/south(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":", …) is an ordinary property reference, so a typo or a renamed room is a compile error, not a broken game."}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let hall = Location {","    name(\"Entrance Hall\")","    description(\"A long hall of grey stone. A doorway opens to the north.\")","}","","let library = Location {","    name(\"Dusty Library\")","    description(\"Shelves sag under mildewed books. The hall lies south.\")","}","","var map: WorldMap {","    hall.north(library)","    library.south(hall)","","    player.starts(in: hall)","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Exits are one-directional by design — declare both "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"hall.north(library)"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"library.south(hall)"},{"type":"text","text":" if you want the player to be able to walk back."}]},{"level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Add-a-thing","text":"Add a thing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Declare an "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Item"},{"type":"text","text":" the same way, then place it in the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"map"},{"type":"text","text":":"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let lantern = Item {","    name(\"brass lantern\")","    adjectives(\"brass\", \"old\")","    description(\"An old brass lantern, its glass sooty but intact.\")","}","","var map: WorldMap {","    hall.north(library)","    library.south(hall)","","    player.starts(in: hall)","    lantern.starts(in: library)","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Now the player can walk "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"north"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"examine lantern"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"take lantern"},{"type":"text","text":", and see it in their "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"inventory"},{"type":"text","text":". The "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/adjectives(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" let them type "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"take brass lantern"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"take old lantern"},{"type":"text","text":"; a phrase has to end on a noun, so "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"take brass"},{"type":"text","text":" on its own is not one of them. The last word of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"name(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" (“lantern”) is the noun the parser keys on."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Everything you declare is split into words the same way the parser splits what the player types — lowercased, a trailing possessive dropped, every other punctuation mark a separator. So "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"name(\"Mrs. Vane\")"},{"type":"text","text":" prints its period and answers to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"mrs vane"},{"type":"text","text":", and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"adjectives(\"master's\")"},{"type":"text","text":" is the same declaration as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"adjectives(\"master\")"},{"type":"text","text":". Write the second: a declaration should read the way the parser stores it."}]},{"level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"React-with-a-rule","text":"React with a rule"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"So far every verb uses its built-in behavior. To add your own logic, write a rule in the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"rules"},{"type":"text","text":" block. Rules are "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"before"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"after"},{"type":"text","text":" hooks attached to a location, an item, or the whole world."}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["var rules: Rules {","    lantern.after(.take) {","        say(\"It's heavier than it looks.\")","    }","","    library.before(.go) {","        guard command.direction != .south else { return }","        try refuse(\"There's no exit that way — only back south to the hall.\")","    }","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The first rule runs "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"after"}]},{"type":"text","text":" the player successfully takes the lantern and adds a line of flavor with "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/say(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":". The second runs "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"before"}]},{"type":"text","text":" movement in the library and "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/refuse(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":"s any direction but south. Inside a rule body, bare identifiers like "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"command"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"player"},{"type":"text","text":", and your own "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"lantern"},{"type":"text","text":" refer to the live turn — reading and writing them touches the current game state."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"To learn what rules can do — the phases, the ordering, and the difference between "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"refuse"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reply"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"say"},{"type":"text","text":", and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"end"},{"type":"text","text":" — read "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/WritingRules"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/TheTurnPipeline"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Test-it","text":"Test it"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A play session is just typed input and printed output, so the natural test plays a scripted session and asserts on the transcript:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["import GnustoTestSupport","import Testing","","@testable import MyGame","","struct MyGameTests {","    @Test func theLanternIsWhereTheBreezeSaysItIs() async throws {","        let transcript = try await play(MyGame(), [\"north\", \"take lantern\"])","        expectInOrder(transcript, [\"Dusty Library\", \"Taken.\"])","    }","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"play"},{"type":"text","text":" boots the game and feeds it each command; "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"expectInOrder"},{"type":"text","text":" asserts the beats appear in order and shows the full transcript when one doesn’t. See "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/TestingYourGame"},{"type":"text","text":" for turn slicing and pinning the random stream."}]},{"level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"A-fuller-example","text":"A fuller example"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Gnusto ships with "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Cloak of Darkness"}]},{"type":"text","text":", Roger Firth’s classic one-room demonstration game, as its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CloakOfDarkness"},{"type":"text","text":" target. It exercises nearly every feature in a page of code — dark rooms, a wearable cloak, scored actions, a losing state, and per-turn rules — and is worth reading start to finish once the basics click."}]},{"level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Next-steps","text":"Next steps"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"bin\/new-game"},{"text":" in the repo — writes the complete starter package this guide builds up to","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/AnatomyOfAGame","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" — how declarations, identity, and live references fit together","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/TheTurnPipeline","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" — exactly what happens each turn","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/WritingRules","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" — the full vocabulary of game logic","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/AddingCustomVerbs","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" — teach the parser new words with ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"#verb"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/TestingYourGame","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" — transcript tests with GnustoTestSupport","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/CustomStateAndTraits","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" — carry your own data on entities and in globals","type":"text"}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"}],"kind":"content"}],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Article","title":"Getting Started with Gnusto","modules":[{"name":"Gnusto"}],"role":"article"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto"]]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Build and run your first text adventure, one piece at a time."}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/AnatomyOfAGame","doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/TheTurnPipeline"],"title":"Essentials","anchor":"Essentials"}],"kind":"article","sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/gnusto\/gettingstarted"]}],"references":{"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto":{"title":"Gnusto","url":"\/documentation\/gnusto","abstract":[{"text":"An engine for writing interactive fiction in Swift.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto","role":"collection","type":"topic"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/WritingRules":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Attach game logic to items, locations, and the world."}],"url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/writingrules","title":"Writing Rules","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/WritingRules","role":"article","type":"topic"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/Location":{"abstract":[{"text":"A place in the world.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/location","title":"Location","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Location"}],"kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Location"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Location","role":"symbol","type":"topic"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/GameWorld":{"url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/gameworld","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The game world: owns all state, serializes all mutation, and runs the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"turn pipeline. The single "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"await"},{"type":"text","text":" in a game sits between the REPL and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"this actor."}],"title":"GameWorld","fragments":[{"text":"actor","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"GameWorld","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"GameWorld","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GameWorld","role":"symbol","type":"topic"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/CustomStateAndTraits":{"abstract":[{"text":"Carry your own data on entities and in globals, alongside the engine’s closed core.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/customstateandtraits","title":"Custom State and Traits","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/CustomStateAndTraits","role":"article","type":"topic"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/say(_:)":{"abstract":[{"text":"Prints a message as part of the turn’s output.","type":"text"}],"title":"say(_:)","url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/say(_:)","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"say"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","text":"String"},{"kind":"text","text":")"}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/say(_:)","role":"symbol","type":"topic"},"getting-started.png":{"variants":[{"url":"\/images\/Gnusto\/getting-started@2x.png","traits":["2x","light"]}],"identifier":"getting-started.png","type":"image","alt":"A lantern lights an open stone doorway and the stairs beyond."},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/IOHandler":{"abstract":[{"text":"Where the game’s text goes and player input comes from. Synchronous by","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"design: a blocking console read is fine for a CLI; an async variant can","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"be added later without breaking this protocol’s clients.","type":"text"}],"title":"IOHandler","url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/iohandler","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"IOHandler","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"IOHandler","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/IOHandler","role":"symbol","type":"topic"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/adjectives(_:)":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Additional words the parser accepts before the item’s noun."}],"url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/adjectives(_:)","title":"adjectives(_:)","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"adjectives"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"String"},{"kind":"text","text":"...) -> "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:6Gnusto9ItemTraitV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"ItemTrait"}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/adjectives(_:)","role":"symbol","type":"topic"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/BootstrapError":{"abstract":[{"text":"All problems with a game definition, reported at once.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/bootstraperror","title":"BootstrapError","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"BootstrapError"}],"kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"BootstrapError"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/BootstrapError","role":"symbol","type":"topic"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/Item":{"abstract":[{"text":"A thing in the world.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/item","title":"Item","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Item"}],"kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Item"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Item","role":"symbol","type":"topic"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/Location/south(_:)":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Location\/south(_:)","title":"south(_:)","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An exit leading south to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"to"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"south"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Location","preciseIdentifier":"s:6Gnusto8LocationV"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"typeIde